# PR #688 self-report accuracy issue: claimed metadata threading through PyNudge
# Actual implementation: hardcoded Platform.TELEGRAM + static ATM_CHAT_ID from env var
# The fix IS functional (test passes) but self-report materially overstates the mechanism.
# Branch: testing/hermes-smoke-testing, commit 9baa734b8b981ab095f8528220260c1c1876649f
# Authored by Cipher-311d, reported by quality-mgr during RBP verification.

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-SELFREPORT-MISMATCH>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-SELFREPORT-MISMATCH" ;
  triage:title "PR #688 self-report overstates implementation mechanism: claims metadata threading, uses hardcoded routing" ;
  triage:description "PR #688 (branch testing/hermes-smoke-testing, commit 9baa734b) to fix AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-GAP claims that 'the graft bridge contract (PyNudge) now carries platform metadata through to the adapter.' Verification: (1) PyNudge struct (crates/atm-graft-python/src/lib.rs:204-245) has three fields only: message_id, source (PyAgentAddress), body. No platform field exists. (2) The actual fix is in crates/atm-graft-python/python/atm_graft_hermes_adapter.py:271, where _dispatch_nudge() uses hardcoded routing: telegram_platform = getattr(Platform, \"TELEGRAM\", Platform.LOCAL) (line 271) plus static self._chat_id sourced once from ATM_CHAT_ID environment variable at __init__ (line 126). This is a fixed single-target design (one Telegram chat per daemon instance), not generalized metadata-threading through the bridge contract. Functional verdict: the fix works (test 12/12 hermes suite pass, 897/0 workspace, 22/22 lint), and the implementation is accurately documented in docs/atm-graft/hermes-agent-use-case.md and docs/plans/phase-ai/hermes-graft-adapter-contract.md, which correctly describe hardcoded routing and do not claim metadata threading. Defect scope: self-report/PR description to delegator only. Impact: the architectural mechanism is not general (will not scale to multi-platform/multi-chat routing), and the misstatement obscures this limitation. Severity: important (misrepresentation of architecture, not a functional bug)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "self-report-accuracy" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-28T12:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI-S3133-HERMES-SMOKE ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-28T12:25:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-SELFREPORT-MISMATCH/hardcoded-telegram-routing> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-SELFREPORT-MISMATCH/pynudge-no-platform> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "testing/hermes-smoke-testing" ;
  triage:promoteTo "testing/hermes-smoke-testing" ;
  triage:rootCause "Self-report describes generalized metadata-threading architecture that does not exist. Actual implementation uses single-target hardcoded routing (Telegram platform + static chat_id from env var), which works for current use case but will not generalize. Architecture limit is real but was not communicated accurately to delegator." ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

